## Model card

- **Name:** Claude Opus 5 (no Free-tier variant found; paid Opus tier. Successor Claude Opus 5.5 released 2026-09-22 — do not conflate.)
- **Short description:** Anthropic's Opus-tier frontier model, announced 2026-07-24 as coming "close to the frontier intelligence of Claude Fable 5 at half the price," positioned for long-running agents, coding, and professional knowledge work. Exposes an adjustable effort setting (high/xhigh/max referenced). Variant flag: distinct from Claude Fable 5, Claude Mythos 5, and the later Claude Opus 5.5.
- **Provider / access:** Anthropic first-party API (announcement: anthropic.com/news/claude-opus-5); Amazon Bedrock (docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/.../model-card-anthropic-claude-opus-5.html); default model on Claude Max, strongest model on Claude Pro. Exact API model string, and Chat Completions vs Responses/Messages API surface: not verified in this session.
- **Release / knowledge:** 2026-07-24 release (Anthropic announcement; system card PDF dated July 24, 2026; TechCrunch/Fortune/Axios same day). Knowledge cutoff: no verified public value found.
- **IDs:** `anthropic/claude-opus-5` (inferred naming, not verified against a live model list). No Free ID found on OpenCode Zen; models.dev / OpenCode Zen entries not verified in this session.
- **Context window:** no verified public value found (not retrieved from official docs before search budget was exhausted).
- **Modalities:** no verified public value found for image/PDF/audio/video input; reasoning: yes (effort setting documented in announcement); tool calls: implied by agentic positioning (Zapier AutomationBench, GDPval-AA) but not verified from docs; JSON mode: not verified.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-09-30):** Paid $. Anthropic states Opus 5 is priced at half of Claude Fable 5 and at the same cost as its predecessor Opus 4.8; Opus 5.5 is stated to cost 40% less than Opus 5 on typical workloads. Absolute $/1M input/output/cached figures: no verified public value found. No free tier → no free-tier privacy caveat applies.
- **Architecture:** Proprietary, closed weights. Parameter count / MoE details: not disclosed.

